# Deployment-specific compose overrides. On the server this is not a file but a
# symlink into /opt/vds-stack/overrides/, and it carries the port mapping and
# the container name — without it the next deploy comes up unreachable behind
# Caddy. Untracked, it appeared in `git status` as a stray file, which is
# precisely what `git clean -fd` removes and precisely what must survive a
# rollback. Ignored, `git clean -fd` leaves it alone. (`git clean -fdx` still
# takes it, and `.env` with it — see "Rolling back" in DEPLOYMENT.md.)
/docker-compose.override.yml

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Local data dumps
/tmp/
*.dump

# The intermediate download the address build script reads. The CSVs under
# apps/address/data are the artefact; these are 9 MB of raw JSON on the way to
# them, and they were committed once already.
/provinces.json
/districts.json
/neighborhoods.json
/villages.json
